      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of somatostatin microinjected bilaterally and unilaterally (left or right) at a dose of 10, 50 and 100 ng into the caudate putamen of male Wistar rats on nociception (analgesy-meter test) were studied. Somatostatin injected into caudate putamen resulted in analgesia. Bilateral microinjections of somatostatin significantly increased the pain threshold in a dose-dependent manner, i.e. somatostatin exerted antinociceptive effect. The pain threshold after left-side microinjections was significantly higher than that after injections into right-side. These findings suggest antinociceptive and asymmetric effects of somatostatin on pain in the caudate putamen."},
